==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|calorique|lang=fr}}, coined by French chemist [[w:Antoine Lavoisier|Antoine Lavoisier]], from {{etyl|la|en}} {{lena}} {{term|calor|lang=la||heat}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|US|UK rare|lang=en}} relating to [[calorie|calories]]
#: ''Caloric intake''
# {{context|US|UK rare|lang=en}} containing calories
#: ''Milk is a caloric beverage.''
#{{context|US|UK rare|lang=en}} high in calories
#: ''A dry, caloric food''
# {{context|US|UK rare|lang=en}} relating to or [[produce|producing]] [[heat]] or other [[energy]]

